From 2c72c88acdf0464789dae56199cba4207d2f9d9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:37:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Export only items whose answers have not come back yet
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Recording a room queues every new item for identification, but nothing
recorded whether a batch had already been sent. If an identifications
file was never imported, `ask` stayed true and the next export resent
the whole backlog — the 2026-10-20 export carried 139 items when only
80 were new.

- stamp `askedAt` on each item actually sent by Export for Claude
- offer, when some of the queue was sent before and no answers have
  been imported since, to send only the items never sent
- show the already-sent count on the Export tab next to "N waiting"
- clear `askedAt` when an answer is imported, alongside `ask`
- carry `askedAt` through saveItem, which rebuilds the item from a
  fixed field list and would otherwise drop it on the next edit

Also adds the Chemicals / Reagents category, which 25 records in the
2026-10-20 batch need, and bumps the version shown in Setup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bv7jkLFHtU5v5fQtRXLizR
